IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-19: Article 19 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): automatically generated logs.
-- Lines 422-425 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Article 19 among the obligations whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- Seam: Article 12(1) (the logs themselves) is P2's; here the logs are a fact the provider states.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, Art 2(13) may limit the Article,
-- the Article limits itself ("to the extent such logs are under their control"), or the text points to other Union or national law outside the sources).

§ `Article 19(1): keeping the logs, "to the extent such logs are under their control", for at least six months`

-- "unless provided otherwise in the applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data": where such a law provides otherwise, the six-month floor
-- is not the text's answer and the period is that law's, which is outside the sources (NOTHING-kind, points outside the text). "Without prejudice to applicable Union or national law" saves that law and adds no condition.
-- "appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system" is a judgment the text states and does not define: a plain input.
-- src:424 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs referred to in Article 12(1), automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems, to the extent such logs are under their control. Without prejudice to applicable Union or national law, the logs shall be kept for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months, unless provided otherwise in the applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data.
@ref Art 19(1) (src:424)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider keeps the logs referred to in Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for which the logs are kept is appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months for which the logs are kept` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1) the provider keeps the logs referred to in Article 12(1) for an appropriate period of at least six months` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such logs are under their control"
        ELSE IF NOT `the provider keeps the logs referred to in Article 12(1)`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs referred to in Article 12(1), automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems" (the logs are under its control and are not kept)
             ELSE IF `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs`
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless provided otherwise in the applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data"
                  ELSE IF `the period for which the logs are kept is appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` AND `the number of months for which the logs are kept` AT LEAST 6
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the logs shall be kept for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 19, "", 0)

§ `Article 19(2): financial institutions maintain the logs as part of the documentation they keep under financial services law`

-- src:425 | 2. Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law.
@ref Art 19(2) (src:425)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 19(2) the provider that is a financial institution has maintained the logs as part of the documentation kept under financial services law` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain" (the provider is not such an institution)
        ELSE
             IF `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 19, "", 0)

@ref Art 19(2) (src:425)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 19 act`
`Art 19(2) the provider's duty to maintain the logs as part of the documentation kept under financial services law` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 19(2) maintain the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the logs were not maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the provider is not a financial institution of that kind
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 19, "", 0)


§ `Regulative rules of Article 19`

DECLARE `Art 19 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 19(1) cease to keep the logs referred to in Article 12(1)`
    `Art 19(2) maintain the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as part of the documentation kept under the relevant financial services law`

-- "the logs shall be kept for a period ... of at least six months": written as a prohibition on ceasing to keep a log during its first six months (the SHANT derived from the flat "shall").
-- The clock is in days from the date asked (day 0, the day the log is generated); the window is the six months counted by `add months`. The rule binds only where the logs are under the
-- provider's control and no other Union or national law provides otherwise.
-- src:424 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs referred to in Article 12(1), automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems, to the extent such logs are under their control. Without prejudice to applicable Union or national law, the logs shall be kept for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months, unless provided otherwise in the applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data.
@ref Art 19(1) (src:424)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 19 act`
`Art 19(1) the provider's duty to keep the logs for at least six months` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control`
         AND NOT `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         SHANT `Art 19(1) cease to keep the logs referred to in Article 12(1)`
         WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date asked` 6)) MINUS (Day `the date asked`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the logs were no longer kept before six months had passed"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the logs are not under the provider's control, or other law provides otherwise
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 19, "", 0)
